1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,514
When your site stores media in Azure Blob Storage or Amazon S3, it

2
00:00:05,514 --> 00:00:08,523
keeps a local copy of the files it serves.

3
00:00:08,523 --> 00:00:13,349
This video enables Media Cache, purges the copy, allows a role to purge

4
00:00:13,349 --> 00:00:16,860
it, and names the tasks that can clean the caches.

5
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:25,782
When media lives in Azure Blob Storage or Amazon S3, your Orchard Core

6
00:00:25,782 --> 00:00:27,375
site serves the files.

7
00:00:27,375 --> 00:00:31,697
The first time someone requests a file, the site downloads it from the

8
00:00:31,697 --> 00:00:34,370
store and keeps a copy on the web server.

9
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:39,955
Later requests for the file use that copy, and image resizing starts from it.

10
00:00:39,955 --> 00:00:44,033
A file you upload in the media library is copied right away, and

11
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:47,120
deleting or moving a file removes its old copy.

12
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:51,625
You purge the whole cache to free disk space or to fetch fresh copies.

13
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:55,282
With a content delivery network in front of your site, you can purge

14
00:00:55,282 --> 00:00:57,950
once the network has fetched the files it needs.

15
00:01:02,143 --> 00:01:05,712
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for Media Cache.

16
00:01:05,712 --> 00:01:10,041
It is in the Content Management category, and its description reads:

17
00:01:10,041 --> 00:01:13,903
The media cache module adds remote file store cache support.

18
00:01:14,354 --> 00:01:19,160
Azure Media Storage and Amazon Media Storage both depend on Media Cache, so

19
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,593
enabling either one enables it too.

20
00:01:21,593 --> 00:01:26,814
Let's enable Media Cache alone, to see what its page shows without a remote store.

21
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:30,980
Settings, Media, Cache opens a page titled Asset Cache.

22
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:35,581
Without a remote store, the page reports an error saying that a remote

23
00:01:35,581 --> 00:01:40,847
media store must be enabled and configured in the host configuration of the site.

24
00:01:45,059 --> 00:01:49,426
On a site where Azure Media Storage is enabled and configured, the same

25
00:01:49,426 --> 00:01:53,850
page shows a notice that media is configured, and one action, Purge All.

26
00:01:53,850 --> 00:01:56,119
It empties the cache of this site.

27
00:01:56,570 --> 00:01:58,151
Let's select Purge All.

28
00:01:58,151 --> 00:01:59,241
A dialog asks:

29
00:01:59,241 --> 00:02:02,510
Are you sure you want to purge the entire asset cache?

30
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:03,600
Let's confirm.

31
00:02:04,134 --> 00:02:06,072
The page shows the message:

32
00:02:06,072 --> 00:02:07,540
Asset cache purged.

33
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:11,063
If a file is in use and the site cannot delete it, the

34
00:02:11,063 --> 00:02:14,116
message reads Asset cache purged, with errors.

35
00:02:14,116 --> 00:02:17,404
The files in the remote store stay where they are.

36
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:20,047
The cache fills again on demand.

37
00:02:20,047 --> 00:02:23,026
Let's request one of the site's images directly.

38
00:02:23,026 --> 00:02:27,330
The site downloads it from the store again, keeps a copy, and serves it.

39
00:02:31,522 --> 00:02:35,998
The Administrator role has the Manage Asset Cache Folder permission.

40
00:02:35,998 --> 00:02:41,382
To give it to another role, open Access Control, Roles, and select Edit for Editor.

41
00:02:41,844 --> 00:02:44,148
Search the permissions for cache.

42
00:02:44,148 --> 00:02:49,052
Under Media Cache, select Allow for Manage Asset Cache Folder, and then Save.

43
00:02:49,052 --> 00:02:52,714
The permission exists only while Media Cache is enabled.

44
00:02:56,914 --> 00:03:00,761
Purge All empties only the copies of the original files.

45
00:03:00,761 --> 00:03:05,724
Resized images are kept in a separate cache, which Purge All leaves alone.

46
00:03:06,474 --> 00:03:09,884
Two background tasks clean the caches on a schedule:

47
00:03:09,884 --> 00:03:13,706
Remote Media Cache Cleaner and Resized Media Cache Cleaner.

48
00:03:13,706 --> 00:03:18,644
With the Background Tasks feature enabled, Tools, Background Tasks lists them.

49
00:03:19,394 --> 00:03:21,422
They run once a day by default.

50
00:03:21,422 --> 00:03:26,574
They do nothing until the host configuration sets a time limit for the cache they clean.

51
00:03:28,574 --> 00:03:32,352
A site that stores media remotely keeps a local copy of it, and

52
00:03:32,352 --> 00:03:35,691
Purge All empties that copy when you need fresh copies.

53
00:03:35,691 --> 00:03:37,114
Thanks for watching.

